-- allium: 3
-- llm-retry-visibility.allium
--
-- LLM Retry Visibility: Behavioural Specification
--
-- Scope: The producer side of LLM-retry visibility — the SSE wire event
--        (LlmAttempt) emitted from the executor's Effect::ScheduleRetry
--        handler, the typed retry context that flows through the
--        envelope, the per-conversation TurnRetryContext entity (read
--        by specs/working-phase-visibility/ to compose the StateBar's
--        retry modifier), and the post-hoc retry_count persisted on the
--        assistant message's display_data.
--
-- Source of truth:
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/api/wire.rs — SseWireEvent::LlmAttempt
--       variant + event_type() tag
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/runtime.rs — SseEvent::LlmAttempt
--       and From<SseEvent> conversion
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/runtime/executor.rs — Effect::ScheduleRetry
--       handler (`executor.rs:1408-1418`); emission site
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/state_machine/transition.rs — retry
--       transitions (handle_core_error_retry, handle_core_continuation);
--       MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS constant
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/llm/error.rs — LlmErrorKind classification
--       (is_retryable)
--
-- Includes: LlmAttemptReason enumeration; the RetryContext value type
--           moved here from working-phase-visibility's PLACEHOLDER block;
--           the TurnRetryContext entity (keyed by conversation_id, like
--           sse_wire's other per-conversation entities); the populator
--           rule (TurnRetryContextUpdatedOnLlmAttempt) and the clear
--           rules (on AgentDone and terminal Error); the post-hoc
--           retry_count persist rule on assistant-message persist.
-- Excludes:
--   - The StateBar rendering of "(retry K/N <reason>)" itself — owned by
--     specs/working-phase-visibility/'s render_retry_modifier_for helper.
--   - The cancellation transitions; modelled in specs/conversation_atom/
--     (the underlying state machine transitions).
--   - The SSE replay-ring eligibility; modelled in specs/sse_wire/'s
--     EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing rule whose whitelist this spec
--     extends.
--
-- Cross-references:
--   specs/working-phase-visibility/working-phase-visibility.allium — the
--       consumer. Imports this spec via `use ".../llm-retry-visibility/
--       llm-retry-visibility.allium" as llm_retry`. Reads
--       llm_retry/TurnRetryContext{conversation_id} via its
--       render_retry_modifier_for helper.
--   specs/sse_wire/sse_wire.allium — wire envelope contract. The
--       `llm_attempt` event_type is added to
--       EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing's whitelist in the same
--       change that lands this spec, per the cross-spec checklist at
--       the top of that rule.
--   specs/conversation_atom/conversation_atom.allium — no atom impact
--       for the wire event itself (it populates a TurnRetryContext
--       entity owned here). The retry_count field on
--       display_data is set at persist time on the existing assistant-
--       message persist path.
--
-- Requirement traceability: REQ-LRV-001 through REQ-LRV-007 are modelled
-- here. REQ-LRV-002 (reason classification) is structurally enforced by
-- the exhaustive match between LlmErrorKind's retryable subset and
-- LlmAttemptReason; modelled via the LlmAttemptReasonClassification rule.
-- REQ-LRV-005 (cancellation routes through Cancelling) is a property of
-- the state machine transitions and the StaleRetryTimeoutAbsorbed
-- behaviour already modelled in specs/conversation_atom/; this spec
-- documents it as a `deferred Req005CancellationDuringBackoff` entry
-- with the rationale.
-- REQ-LRV-007 (LlmAttempt vs RateLimitSnapshot distinct) is a wire-level
-- contract enforced by the sse_wire replay-ring whitelist; modelled
-- here as the LlmAttemptReplayEligible invariant cross-referencing
-- sse_wire.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Why a retry attempt is being scheduled. Mirrors the retryable subset
-- of LlmErrorKind exactly (`llm/error.rs:111` — Network, RateLimit,
-- ServerError). Non-retryable LlmErrorKind variants terminate the turn
-- without scheduling a retry, so they never reach this enum.
value LlmAttemptReason {
    -- one of: rate_limit, server_error, network
    -- (declared as an enum in the implementation; Allium v3 grammar
    -- represents the three-value distinction via the equality
    -- predicates in the rules below)
    kind: String
}

-- The retry context surfaced to the client for one in-flight retry.
-- Moved here from working-phase-visibility's PLACEHOLDER block on
-- this spec's landing. Carries everything the consumer's
-- render_retry_modifier_for(view) helper needs to compose the
-- "(retry K/N <reason>)" suffix, plus informational fields
-- (backing_off_ms, resets_at) for future displays.
--
-- Field semantics:
--   attempt:        The attempt number this retry is scheduled FOR.
--                   1-indexed; matches the state's `attempt` after
--                   the bump.
--   max_attempts:   The retry-budget ceiling
--                   (MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3 in
--                   `state_machine/transition.rs:183`). Carried
--                   per-event so a future per-provider policy is
--                   wire-compatible.
--   reason:         Classified per LlmAttemptReasonClassification.
--   reason_text:    Human-rendered form of `reason` ("rate limit",
--                   "server error", "network error"). Set by
--                   the populator rule from a shared helper
--                   reason_to_text(reason).
--   backing_off_ms: The retry-delay value from
--                   Effect::ScheduleRetry, in milliseconds.
--                   Informational at v1 — no rule depends on it.
--   resets_at:      Quota reset timestamp from LlmError.quota when
--                   the error was a RateLimit with quota details;
--                   null otherwise.
value RetryContext {
    attempt:        Integer
    max_attempts:   Integer
    reason:         LlmAttemptReason
    reason_text:    String
    backing_off_ms: Integer
    resets_at:      Timestamp?
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Per-conversation retry context for the current turn. Keyed by
-- conversation_id (the same pattern sse_wire, conn, and
-- conversation_atom use for per-conversation state); a single tab
-- maps a conversation_id to its ClientView via the working-phase-
-- visibility's helpers when rendering. Cleared on turn-terminal
-- events (AgentDone, terminal Error) by the rules below.
--
-- Population is the producer-side observation of a server-emitted
-- LlmAttempt event; the entity's lifecycle is bounded by the turn,
-- not by the SSE connection (a reconnect mid-turn replays the
-- LlmAttempt via the ephemeral ring and re-populates the entity —
-- see LlmAttemptReplayEligible invariant).
entity TurnRetryContext {
    conversation_id: String
    retry:           RetryContext
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers (pure functions referenced by the rules below)
------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Allium has no formal helper-function declaration; the rules below
-- call these by bare identifier. This block is the single source of
-- truth for their signatures and semantics. Any rule that uses a name
-- not in this block is using an undeclared helper — call that out in
-- review.
--
--   classify_retry_reason(error_kind: LlmErrorKind) -> LlmAttemptReason
--       Maps the retryable subset of LlmErrorKind to LlmAttemptReason:
--           Network     -> LlmAttemptReason{kind: "network"}
--           RateLimit   -> LlmAttemptReason{kind: "rate_limit"}
--           ServerError -> LlmAttemptReason{kind: "server_error"}
--       Undefined on non-retryable variants (which never reach
--       Effect::ScheduleRetry per is_retryable() in llm/error.rs:111).
--
--   reason_to_text(reason: LlmAttemptReason) -> String
--       Maps reason.kind to its human-rendered form:
--           "rate_limit"   -> "rate limit"
--           "server_error" -> "server error"
--           "network"      -> "network error"
--       The strings are not normative wire syntax; they are the
--       implementation's single source of truth and are referenced by
--       working-phase-visibility's render_retry_modifier_for helper
--       to compose " (retry K/N <reason_text>)".
--
--   state_attempt(conv_id: String) -> Integer
--       The attempt counter from the conversation's current
--       ConvState (LlmRequesting or AwaitingContinuation). The
--       runtime guarantees state.attempt == LlmAttempt.attempt on
--       every retry-scheduled emission (the state is bumped in the
--       same transition that schedules the retry — see
--       handle_core_error_retry / handle_core_continuation in
--       transition.rs).
--
--   max_retry_attempts() -> Integer
--       The global retry-budget ceiling. Sourced from
--       `state_machine/transition.rs::MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`. Returned
--       as a value so any future per-provider policy can switch the
--       implementation without changing the wire shape.
--
------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — LlmAttempt classification + emission
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-LRV-002: the runtime-side classification of LlmErrorKind to
-- LlmAttemptReason. Documents the contract that the wire emission
-- (RuntimeEmitsLlmAttemptOnScheduleRetry below) honors. Modelling this
-- as a rule (rather than @guidance) makes the three-way mapping
-- structural: if a future LlmErrorKind variant becomes retryable, the
-- match here must be extended or the rule is incomplete.
--
-- Event shape: RuntimeClassifiesRetryError(conv_id, error_kind).
-- Fires inside handle_core_error_retry / handle_core_continuation at
-- the moment the rule's `if error_kind.is_retryable() && *attempt <
-- MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS` guard passes.
rule LlmAttemptReasonClassification {
    when: RuntimeClassifiesRetryError(conv_id, error_kind)

    -- The three retryable variants in LlmErrorKind. The runtime
    -- guarantees this rule fires only inside the retryable guard, so
    -- the four non-retryable variants (UsageLimitReached,
    -- ServerOverloaded, Auth, InvalidRequest, ContentFilter,
    -- ContextWindowExceeded) never trigger.
    requires: error_kind in { "network", "rate_limit", "server_error" }

    let reason = classify_retry_reason(error_kind)

    ensures: ClassifiedRetryReason{conv_id}.reason = reason
}

-- REQ-LRV-001: the SSE wire emission. Fires from the executor's
-- Effect::ScheduleRetry handler (`executor.rs:1408-1418`),
-- immediately before the spawned tokio sleep that drives the
-- backoff. The emission and the sleep happen in the same effect
-- arm, so there is no ordering window in which the sleep
-- completes (and a RetryTimeout outcome lands) before the
-- LlmAttempt event has been queued for broadcast.
--
-- Event shape: EffectScheduleRetryEmitted(conv_id, attempt, delay_ms,
--                                          reason, resets_at).
rule RuntimeEmitsLlmAttemptOnScheduleRetry {
    when: EffectScheduleRetryEmitted(conv_id, attempt, delay_ms, reason, resets_at)

    requires: attempt >= 1
    requires: attempt <= max_retry_attempts()
    requires: reason.kind in { "network", "rate_limit", "server_error" }
    requires: delay_ms >= 0

    -- The LlmAttempt event is constructed here. The actual SSE
    -- envelope (sequence_id assignment, broadcast) is the sse_wire
    -- responsibility; this rule constructs the payload value.
    let payload = RetryContext{
        attempt:        attempt,
        max_attempts:   max_retry_attempts(),
        reason:         reason,
        reason_text:    reason_to_text(reason),
        backing_off_ms: delay_ms,
        resets_at:      resets_at
    }

    ensures: LlmAttemptBroadcast{conv_id}.payload = payload

    @guidance
        -- Implementation: inside the Effect::ScheduleRetry arm of
        -- ConversationRuntime::handle_effect, prior to the
        -- tokio::spawn that schedules the backoff sleep:
        --
        --   let _ = self.broadcast_tx.send_seq(|seq| SseEvent::LlmAttempt {
        --       sequence_id: seq,
        --       attempt,
        --       max_attempts: MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS,
        --       reason,
        --       backing_off_ms: delay.as_millis() as u64,
        --       resets_at,
        --   });
        --
        -- The `reason` and `resets_at` arguments to Effect::ScheduleRetry
        -- are added in the same change. handle_core_error_retry and
        -- handle_core_continuation in transition.rs build them from the
        -- inbound Event::LlmError's error_kind + (newly-added) resets_at
        -- fields. resets_at is non-null only for RateLimit errors whose
        -- LlmError.quota carries a resets_at value.
        --
        -- Replay eligibility: the LlmAttempt event IS appended to the
        -- ephemeral replay ring (sse_wire's EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing
        -- whitelist includes "llm_attempt"). Without this, a client
        -- reconnecting mid-backoff would lose the retry context
        -- (REQ-LRV-001 rationale).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — TurnRetryContext lifecycle
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-LRV-001 / REQ-LRV-003: the client-side population. When the
-- client receives an LlmAttempt event, the TurnRetryContext for the
-- conversation is created or replaced. Replaced (not merged) because
-- each attempt's context fully supersedes the previous one —
-- "(retry 2/3 after 429)" is replaced by "(retry 3/3 after server
-- error)" if the second retry hits a different error class.
--
-- Event shape: SseLlmAttemptReceived(conv_id, attempt, max_attempts,
--                                     reason, backing_off_ms, resets_at).
rule TurnRetryContextUpdatedOnLlmAttempt {
    when: SseLlmAttemptReceived(conv_id, attempt, max_attempts, reason, backing_off_ms, resets_at)

    let payload = RetryContext{
        attempt:        attempt,
        max_attempts:   max_attempts,
        reason:         reason,
        reason_text:    reason_to_text(reason),
        backing_off_ms: backing_off_ms,
        resets_at:      resets_at
    }

    ensures: TurnRetryContext{conv_id}.retry = payload
}

-- REQ-LRV-003 (cross-spec) / REQ-WPV-003 (per the consumer): the
-- retry context lives across intra-turn phase transitions
-- (llm_requesting -> tool_executing carries the retry suffix
-- forward; see working-phase-visibility's REQ-WPV-003 example
-- "executing bash 12s (retry 2/5)"). It is cleared only at the
-- turn boundary. AgentDone is the success-path boundary.
--
-- Event shape: SseAgentDoneReceived(conv_id).
-- (Moved here from working-phase-visibility on this spec's landing;
-- the consumer no longer owns the entity.)
rule TurnRetryContextClearedOnAgentDone {
    when: SseAgentDoneReceived(conv_id)

    requires: exists TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}

    ensures: not exists TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}
}

-- The error-path boundary. A terminal UserFacingError (mapped from a
-- non-retryable LlmErrorKind, or from a retryable kind that hit
-- MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS, or from a tool failure that aborts the turn)
-- concludes the retry visibility. Surfacing "(retry 2/3)" alongside a
-- finalised error message is confusing — the user reads it as "still
-- retrying" when in fact the turn has given up.
--
-- Event shape: SseErrorReceived(conv_id).
rule TurnRetryContextClearedOnTerminalError {
    when: SseErrorReceived(conv_id)

    requires: exists TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}

    ensures: not exists TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — post-hoc retry_count persistence
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-LRV-006: when an assistant message is persisted for a turn
-- that retried at least once, the final retry count is captured on
-- the message's display_data.retry_count field. The badge
-- "(retried Nx)" is rendered by the UI when retry_count > 0.
--
-- The runtime captures the final attempt count from the state being
-- transitioned out of (LlmRequesting{attempt: N} or
-- AwaitingContinuation{attempt: N}) at the moment LlmResponse fires.
-- retry_count = max(0, final_attempt - 1): a turn that succeeded on
-- the first try has final_attempt = 1 and retry_count = 0 (badge
-- hidden); a turn that succeeded on the third try has final_attempt
-- = 3 and retry_count = 2 (badge reads "(retried 2x)").
--
-- Event shape: AssistantMessagePersisted(conv_id, message_id,
--                                         final_attempt).
rule RetryCountPersistedAtTurnEnd {
    when: AssistantMessagePersisted(conv_id, message_id, final_attempt)

    requires: final_attempt >= 1

    -- max(0, final_attempt - 1). Allium v3 has no built-in max; the
    -- helper is left as a runtime-side detail (retry_count is
    -- floor-clamped to 0 — final_attempt is always >= 1 in
    -- practice because the state machine bumps it on every retry,
    -- starting from 1 on the first request, so the subtraction never
    -- underflows).
    let count = final_attempt - 1

    ensures: PersistedAssistantMessage{message_id}.display_data_retry_count = count

    @guidance
        -- Implementation: inside the Effect::persist_agent_message
        -- handler (`state_machine/transition.rs` -- search for the
        -- persist path), or the Effect::PersistCheckpoint path for
        -- turns ending in a tool round, capture
        --   final_attempt = current_attempt(&state)
        -- at the moment of the LlmResponse transition. Write
        --   message.display_data.retry_count = final_attempt - 1
        -- on the assistant message. retry_count is a typed
        -- field on the MessageDisplayData struct (Rust-side); ts-rs
        -- codegen exports the field to TypeScript.
        --
        -- For rollout, the field is gated by `#[serde(default)]` so
        -- existing assistant message rows (which predate the field)
        -- read as retry_count = 0. The UI's badge-display rule
        -- (retry_count > 0) hides the badge for those rows, which
        -- is correct: we have no record of retries on legacy rows.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-LRV-001 + REQ-WPV-008: the LlmAttempt event must replay on
-- reconnect so the StateBar's retry suffix is preserved across the
-- disconnect. This is enforced cross-spec by sse_wire's
-- EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing rule (whose event_type
-- whitelist includes "llm_attempt"). The invariant here is the
-- consumer-side property: if the producer emitted LlmAttempt and
-- the conversation has not yet hit a turn-boundary clear,
-- TurnRetryContext exists for the conversation.
invariant TurnRetryContextPresentBetweenAttemptAndTurnBoundary {
    -- "If an LlmAttempt was the most recent retry-relevant event for
    -- a conversation and no turn-boundary clear has fired since,
    -- TurnRetryContext exists for that conversation."
    -- Modelled as a property of the rule fan-in: the populator rule
    -- sets it; the two clear rules unset it; no other rule touches
    -- it. The implementation guarantees this by construction.
    for conv_id in TurnRetryContext:
        TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}.retry.attempt >= 1
        and TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}.retry.attempt
              <= TurnRetryContext{conversation_id: conv_id}.retry.max_attempts
}

-- REQ-LRV-002: the wire emission only carries reason values from the
-- retryable subset. Structurally enforced by the
-- RuntimeEmitsLlmAttemptOnScheduleRetry rule's reason.kind precondition.
invariant LlmAttemptReasonInRetryableSet {
    for conv_id in LlmAttemptBroadcast:
        LlmAttemptBroadcast{conv_id}.payload.reason.kind
            in { "network", "rate_limit", "server_error" }
}

-- REQ-LRV-004: LlmAttempt is emitted on the conversation whose
-- state machine scheduled the retry. Sub-agents have their own
-- conversation_id and their own SSE stream; the runtime guarantees
-- broadcast scope (broadcast_tx is per-conversation). The invariant
-- documents the contract:
invariant LlmAttemptDoesNotEscapeConversationBoundary {
    -- "An LlmAttempt for conversation X is delivered only on
    -- conversation X's SSE stream."
    -- Modelled as a sse_wire-level property; this spec asserts the
    -- non-leak by construction of broadcast_tx scope.
    for conv_id in LlmAttemptBroadcast:
        LlmAttemptBroadcast{conv_id}.delivered_on_conversation = conv_id
}

-- REQ-LRV-007: LlmAttempt is replay-eligible; RateLimitSnapshot is
-- not. The invariant restates the wire-level contract from
-- sse_wire.allium's EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing whitelist
-- (which includes "llm_attempt" and excludes "rate_limit_snapshot").
-- Modelled here as a cross-spec assertion so a future change to
-- either spec that breaks the invariant surfaces in this spec's
-- check rather than only in sse_wire's.
invariant LlmAttemptReplayEligible {
    -- "Every LlmAttempt event appended to a conversation's replay
    -- ring is later observable to a reconnecting client via the
    -- ring's pending_events on the next InitSnapshot."
    -- This is the contract; the realisation is in sse_wire's
    -- EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing rule (whose whitelist
    -- includes "llm_attempt"). Stated here so a future change that
    -- drops "llm_attempt" from the whitelist breaks an invariant
    -- visibly attributed to this spec.
    -- (Truly structural assertion would require a cross-spec entity
    -- reference; the prose form is the load-bearing reminder for
    -- now — see `deferred ReplayRingMembershipStructural` below.)
    true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The two surfaces this spec exposes:
--
--   RetryContextProducer — read by working-phase-visibility's
--       render_retry_modifier_for(view) helper. Exposes the
--       TurnRetryContext entity (keyed by conversation_id) and
--       the RetryContext value type.
--
--   RetryCountPersistedSurface — read by the UI's
--       AssistantMessage component to render the post-hoc badge.
--       Exposes the display_data.retry_count field on a persisted
--       assistant message.
surface RetryContextProducer {
    facing consumer_conversation: String

    exposes:
        TurnRetryContext{conversation_id}
        RetryContext

    @guarantee TurnBoundaryClears
        -- TurnRetryContext is removed on every turn-terminal event
        -- (AgentDone, terminal Error). The consumer is guaranteed
        -- not to render a stale "(retry K/N)" suffix on a turn that
        -- has finished or aborted.

    @guarantee RetryablesOnly
        -- The reason field is always one of the three retryable
        -- classifications (Network, RateLimit, ServerError). Non-
        -- retryable LlmErrorKind variants never produce an
        -- LlmAttempt because the state machine terminates the turn
        -- without scheduling a retry.

    @guarantee ReplaySurvivable
        -- A client reconnecting mid-backoff observes the LlmAttempt
        -- via the SSE replay ring and reconstructs TurnRetryContext
        -- identical to a continuously-connected client's. The
        -- guarantee is rooted in sse_wire's
        -- EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing whitelist; this surface
        -- asserts the consumer-visible consequence.
}

surface RetryCountPersistedSurface {
    facing message_consumer: String  -- message_id

    exposes:
        PersistedAssistantMessage{message_id}.display_data_retry_count

    @guarantee NonNegativeRetryCount
        -- retry_count is always >= 0. Zero means "did not retry" and
        -- the UI's badge-display rule hides the badge in that case.

    @guarantee CountIsFinalAttemptMinusOne
        -- retry_count = final_attempt - 1 for the LlmResponse that
        -- produced the persisted message. The runtime captures
        -- final_attempt at the moment of state transition out of
        -- LlmRequesting/AwaitingContinuation.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred PerProviderRetryPolicies
    -- All retryable LlmErrorKind variants share the global
    -- MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3 ceiling (`state_machine/transition.rs:183`)
    -- and the exponential backoff 1s/2s/4s. Per-provider customisation
    -- (e.g. longer backoff for Anthropic 429, faster for OpenAI 5xx)
    -- is wire-compatible — the LlmAttempt event carries max_attempts
    -- per-event, so the runtime can switch policies without a spec
    -- change. Defer until a use case materialises.
    -- Location: crates/phoenix-ide/src/state_machine/transition.rs

deferred LiveBackoffCountdown
    -- A live "backing off Ns" sub-display would compose
    -- (now() - llm_attempt.event_arrived_at) against
    -- llm_attempt.backing_off_ms to show the remaining backoff.
    -- The wire field is already present; the consumer-side rule
    -- would live in specs/working-phase-visibility/ as a new
    -- DisplayWhen* rule gated on "currently backing off." V1 omits
    -- this; the static "(retry K/N <reason>)" suffix is sufficient.
    -- Location: ui/src/components/StateBar.tsx

deferred CrossConversationRetryRollup
    -- A parent-view aggregation ("this parent's sub-agents are
    -- collectively retrying") is potentially useful for the
    -- aggregate-dashboard feature but out of scope for v1. The
    -- per-conversation TurnRetryContext entity is the precondition
    -- for any such rollup.
    -- Location: would live in ui/src/pages/

deferred PerToolRetryBadge
    -- An inline badge on a tool widget ("this tool call's underlying
    -- LLM turn retried 2x") would require correlating LlmAttempt
    -- events to specific tool blocks. The retry_count on the
    -- assistant-message persist (REQ-LRV-006) covers the post-hoc
    -- message-level surface; per-tool granularity is deferred.
    -- See working-phase-visibility's PerArtifactRetryBadge deferred
    -- entry — the two are linked.
    -- Location: ui/src/components/MessageComponents.tsx

deferred Req005CancellationDuringBackoff
    -- REQ-LRV-005 is satisfied by the existing state machine: a
    -- user-triggered cancel during backoff transitions the
    -- conversation to a Cancelling* variant (handled by
    -- handle_core_cancel paths); the spawned Effect::ScheduleRetry
    -- task continues sleeping but its eventual RetryTimeout event is
    -- absorbed by the state machine's idle-LlmResponse stale-event
    -- absorber (the `Idle`+`LlmResponse` stale absorber in
    -- transition.rs). The display side naturally tracks the
    -- transition via the same TurnRetryContext entity (cleared on
    -- the turn-terminal event that follows the cancellation, per
    -- TurnRetryContextClearedOn{AgentDone,TerminalError} rules
    -- above). No new event or rule needed; the requirement is the
    -- explicit documentation of this behaviour.
    -- Location: specs/conversation_atom/ (state machine transitions)

deferred ReplayRingMembershipStructural
    -- The LlmAttemptReplayEligible invariant above is asserted as
    -- prose because cross-spec entity membership is awkward to
    -- express structurally in Allium v3. A future extension could
    -- model sse_wire/ReplayRing.entries explicitly across specs and
    -- assert that every LlmAttemptBroadcast{conv_id} appears in the
    -- corresponding ring. For v1 the cross-spec checklist at the
    -- top of EphemeralEventAppendedToReplayRing is the operational
    -- safeguard.
    -- Location: specs/sse_wire/sse_wire.allium

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open questions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- No open questions remain. Decisions resolved during drafting
-- (session of 2026-05-27):
--
--   - LlmAttempt vs RateLimitSnapshot: kept distinct (REQ-LRV-007).
--     LlmAttempt IS replay-eligible; RateLimitSnapshot is NOT.
--     Different lifecycles, different staleness properties.
--
--   - max_attempts source: global MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS = 3
--     (`transition.rs:183`). Per-event field on the wire keeps the
--     contract per-provider-compatible for the future.
--
--   - resets_at threading: widen Event::LlmError to carry
--     resets_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>> (sourced from
--     LlmError.quota.resets_at on the inbound error). The retry
--     scheduler forwards it onto Effect::ScheduleRetry and from
--     there onto the LlmAttempt wire event. Alternative
--     (side-channel quota-store lookup at emit time) rejected for
--     coupling the executor to codex-specific quota state.
--
--   - retry_count carrier on the persisted message: typed
--     `retry_count: u32` field on MessageDisplayData. Mirrors
--     working-phase-visibility's tool_starts and the existing
--     duration_ms-on-tool-result convention. Rejected: a new SSE
--     variant (parallel representation), a free-form JSON key
--     (loss of compile-time shape).
--
--   - Sub-agent retries: parent stays mute (REQ-LRV-004). Each
--     conversation's SSE stream carries only its own retries.
--     Cross-conversation rollups deferred.
--
--   - Cancellation during backoff: no new event needed — the
--     existing Cancelling* transitions are the abort signal, stale
--     RetryTimeouts are filtered by the state machine's idle
--     absorber. The display naturally tracks the transition
--     through the same TurnRetryContext lifecycle. Documented
--     explicitly as Req005CancellationDuringBackoff deferred.
--
--   - Backing-off countdown: deferred (LiveBackoffCountdown). V1
--     renders only the static "(retry K/N <reason>)" suffix; the
--     backing_off_ms wire field exists for the future countdown
--     and for log/debug visibility.
